# Gitignored files/dirs to copy into new worktrees created by `claude -w`.
# Syntax: .gitignore-style patterns. Only files that are gitignored AND match
# a pattern get copied; tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# Why each entry exists:
# - `.claude/skills/<name>/` and `.codex/skills/<name>/` are junctions pointing
#   to the SSOT repo. They are gitignored and
#   would not be inherited by fresh git worktree checkouts. Worktree session
#   needs them to invoke /<skill> without manual /sync-skill-from-SSOT
#   (which is itself a junction — chicken-and-egg).
# - `.agents/skills/` is where Codex looks for repo-scope skills. Unlike the
#   entries above it holds real files, not junctions: the Matt skill set is
#   installed there and gitignored, and there is no USER-scope copy for Codex
#   to fall back on (Claude Code is unaffected — it loads that set from a
#   user-level plugin cache). Without this entry a fresh worktree's Codex
#   agent has no Matt skills at all. The pattern covers the whole directory
#   on purpose: naming skills one by one would silently miss whatever
#   upstream adds next.
.agents/skills/
